{
 "regions": [
  {
   "id": "r2",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "factory, and proposes that विशेष should be taken to mean 'great-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "ness,' उत्कर्ष. This is certainly no improvement on Râmarshi's",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "interpretation which is quite unobjectionable and gives good",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "sense. The fig. is अर्थान्तरन्यास.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "Sl. 55. फलं-बिसं v. l. is not appropriate. शयन–a bed or",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "couch; fr. शी + ल्युट् ( अन ) added अधिकरणे. Cf. शय्या च भूः sl. 16",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "supra; also 27, 95. नवधन &c.—upstart wealth often produces",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "intoxication. अनुमन्तुम्—to consent to, to tolerate. Cf, for",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "the idea, infra sl. 27.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "Sl. 56. This sl. gives expression to the thoughts of some",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "one disgusted with royal service. अशीमहिः—for अश्नीमहि. आशा",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "( the quarters ) एव वास; cf. दिगम्बर.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "Sl. 57. विटाः—flatterers, panderers. In dramas this word",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "has a technical meaning. It means the companion of the hero",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "or a king who is skilled in one art only. See com. गायनाः—ल्युट्",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "( अन ) added कर्तरि. नृपस०—A king's palace is frequented by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "buffoons, flatterers, and licentious and malicious people. The",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "poet says, as he is none of these, a royal court is not the place",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "for him. Mr. Telang here quotes from Juvenal the following",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 10,
     "text": "parallel lines:—",
     "end": "line"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "“ What's Rome to me, what business have I there ?",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "I who can neither lie, nor falsely swear,",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "Nor praise my patron's underserving rhymes. ”",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "Sl. 58 विपुलहृदय—large-hearted, generous–minded–refers to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "Brahmá and other Prajápatis, or to Brahmá alone, the pl. being",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "used आदरे. विधृतम्—upheld, preserved–refers to Vishṇu and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "others or to Vishṇu alone. दत्तं &c.—probably a reference to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "Paras'uráma, who conquered the world, and presented it to the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "Bráhmaṇas. कतिपय &c.—when supremacy has been acquired",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "over a few towns. मदज्वर-Cf. ज्वर इव मदो मे. Nî. sl. 8.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "Sl. 59. अभुक्तायां &c.—The sovereign is considered as the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "husband of the earth by Sanskṛt poets. Cf. ना विष्णुः पृथिवीपतिः",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "where the king is spoken of as the husband of the earth. क इव",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "बहुमानः—what honour is it, indeed ? इव being used for emphasis",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
